        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2025/06/apple-wallet-app-ios-26.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple Wallet keeps adding support for new car key brands, with recent additions like <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/02/17/car-keys-in-apple-wallet-just-launched-for-a-major-new-automaker/\">Toyota</a> and <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/14/car-keys-in-apple-wallet-now-available-for-a-major-new-vehicle-brand/\">Porsche</a>. Now, another popular automaker is reportedly about to get car keys: Volkswagen.</p>",
