        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/01/ios-27-just-broke-15-years-of-muscle-memory-on-iphone-and-ipad/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/06/siri-ipad-ios-27-notification-siri.webp?w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Since iOS 5 in 2011, the iPhone and iPad have included Notification Center, a central place to find alerts from various apps in chronological order.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Starting with iOS 27, Apple is making a major change to how users open Notification Center on iPhone and iPad. iOS 27 is currently in beta, and the behavior has changed slightly between the first two releases.</p>",
